{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git ls-files -v game/games/lanterns/.scene/*; git check-ignore -v game/games/lanterns/.scene/scene.binhex game/games/lanterns/artifacts/proof.txt || true; wc -c game/games/lanterns/.scene/*; git diff --numstat -- game/games/lanterns/fixtures/difficult-moment.continuations.jsonl; sed -n '1,90p' game/games/lanterns/README.md; git diff -- game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"game/.gitignore:6:/games/*/.scene/\tgame/games/lanterns/.scene/scene.binhex\ngame/.gitignore:3:/games/*/artifacts/\tgame/games/lanterns/artifacts/proof.txt\n 37146 game/games/lanterns/.scene/scene.binhex\n 37259 game/games/lanterns/.scene/scene.contract\n 78628 game/games/lanterns/.scene/scene.map.json\n153033 total\n605\t605\tgame/games/lanterns/fixtures/difficult-moment.continuations.jsonl\n# Lanterns Exact\n\nA three-minute third-person game built on Exact's game add-on. Move the animated\nFox with WASD, arrows, or the left side of a touch screen. Jump with Space or the\npurple button and press E or LIGHT within 1.5 metres of a lantern. Push the crate\nto reach the twelfth lantern on the ledge.\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh test\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh proof\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh build-web\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh dev\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh macos\nsh game/games/lanterns/run.sh ios\n```\n\nThe original Fox.glb from Khronos glTF Sample Models remains unchanged; its\nattribution and licence are next to the asset. Game state, Rapier bodies, input,\ntimer, lanterns, and current animation clip are all included in Exact world saves.\n\n`build-web` also injects the development-only `window.lanterns.command` adapter\nused by the independent comparison harness. It is inert unless the URL contains\n`?agent=1`; the adapter sends platform input into the real Exact surface, advances\nExact's owned clock, and persists the surface's public save carrier in localStorage.\n\nInitial terrain and the thirteen-lantern roster live in `scene.json`; repeated lantern\nparts live in `lantern.fragment.json`. Run `bun game/dev.mjs lanterns --scene-only`\nafter content edits, or add `--reuse-baker` to skip Cargo completely once the typed\nbaker exists. Rust behavior remains unchanged. Restart uses the new content;\nContinue/Restore keeps saved progress. See [typed scene usage](../../scene/README.md)\nfor parameters, overrides, asset validation and digest-bound development source links.\ndiff --git a/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs b/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\nindex fa98adf..9b9e1ab 100644\n--- a/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\n+++ b/game/games/lanterns/logic/src/lib.rs\n@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ pub struct Lanterns;\n impl Game for Lanterns {\n     const CAPTURE_SUPPORTED: bool = true;\n     const ID: &'static str = \"lanterns\";\n-    const SAVE_VERSION: u32 = 2;\n+    const SAVE_VERSION: u32 = 3;\n     type Args = Options;\n \n     fn assets() -> &'static [Asset] {\n@@ -541,6 +541,8 @@ mod tests {\n     use super::*;\n     use exact_game::Sim;\n \n+    const STEP_MS: f64 = 1000.0 / 60.0;\n+\n     fn game() -> Sim<Lanterns> {\n         Sim::new(Options {\n             scene: bake_scene().content,\n@@ -552,11 +554,55 @@ mod tests {\n         .unwrap()\n     }\n \n+    fn drive_to(sim: &mut Sim<Lanterns>, target: Vec2) {\n+        let mut held = [false; 4];\n+        let keys = [\"KeyA\", \"KeyD\", \"KeyW\", \"KeyS\"];\n+        for _ in 0..1_200 {\n+            let position = sim.world().get::<Transform>(\"player\").unwrap().position;\n+            let delta = target - Vec2::new(position.x, position.z);\n+            if delta.x.abs() < 0.08 && delta.y.abs() < 0.08 {\n+                for (down, key) in held.iter_mut().zip(keys) {\n+                    if *down {\n+                        sim.key_up(key);\n+                        *down = false;\n+                    }\n+                }\n+                return;\n+            }\n+            let wanted = [\n+                delta.x < -0.08,\n+                delta.x > 0.08,\n+                delta.y < -0.08,\n+                delta.y > 0.08,\n+            ];\n+            for ((down, want), key) in held.iter_mut().zip(wanted).zip(keys) {\n+                if *down != want {\n+                    if want {\n+                        sim.key_down(key);\n+                    } else {\n+                        sim.key_up(key);\n+                    }\n+                    *down = want;\n+                }\n+            }\n+            sim.run(STEP_MS);\n+        }\n+        panic!(\n+            \"ordinary movement did not reach {target:?}; stopped at {:?}\",\n+            sim.world().get::<Transform>(\"player\").unwrap().position\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n+    fn act(sim: &mut Sim<Lanterns>) {\n+        sim.tap(\"KeyE\");\n+        sim.run(STEP_MS);\n+    }\n+\n     #[test]\n-    fn level_has_matching_player_crate_obstacles_and_twelve_targets() {\n+    fn level_has_matching_player_crate_obstacles_and_thirteen_targets() {\n         let sim = game();\n         let world = sim.world();\n-        assert_eq!(world.rows::<Lamp>().count(), 12);\n+        assert_eq!(world.rows::<Lamp>().count(), 13);\n         assert_eq!(\n             world.get::<Transform>(\"crate\").unwrap().position,\n             Vec3::new(6.0, 0.6, 8.0)\n@@ -565,6 +611,14 @@ mod tests {\n             world.get::<Transform>(\"lantern-12\").unwrap().position,\n             Vec3::new(10.0, 2.4, 8.0)\n         );\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            world.get::<Transform>(\"raised-platform\").unwrap().position,\n+            Vec3::new(-8.0, 0.6, 7.0)\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            world.get::<Transform>(\"lantern-13\").unwrap().position,\n+            Vec3::new(-8.0, 1.2, 7.0)\n+        );\n         assert!(world.has::<Animation>(world.named(\"fox\").unwrap()));\n     }\n \n@@ -599,6 +653,65 @@ mod tests {\n         );\n     }\n \n+    #[test]\n+    fn ordinary_input_reaches_raised_lantern_only_after_jump_and_twelve_do_not_win() {\n+        let mut sim = game();\n+        for (name, target) in [\n+            (\"lantern-11\", Vec2::new(0.0, 7.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-10\", Vec2::new(0.0, 0.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-9\", Vec2::new(5.0, 2.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-8\", Vec2::new(12.0, 0.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-7\", Vec2::new(12.0, -8.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-6\", Vec2::new(6.0, -12.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-5\", Vec2::new(0.0, -10.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-4\", Vec2::new(-6.0, -12.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-3\", Vec2::new(-12.0, -8.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-2\", Vec2::new(-10.0, 2.0)),\n+            (\"lantern-1\", Vec2::new(-12.0, 10.0)),\n+        ] {\n+            drive_to(&mut sim, target);\n+            act(&mut sim);\n+            assert!(sim.world().get::<Lantern>(name).unwrap().lit, \"{name}\");\n+        }\n+\n+        // The closest legal ground position is outside the solid platform, so\n+        // the 1.2 m elevation combines with that horizontal gap to prevent a\n+        // remote interaction from below.\n+        drive_to(&mut sim, Vec2::new(-8.0, 9.3));\n+        act(&mut sim);\n+        assert!(!sim.world().get::<Lantern>(\"lantern-13\").unwrap().lit);\n+\n+        sim.key_down(\"KeyW\");\n+        sim.tap(\"Space\");\n+        sim.run(350.0);\n+        sim.key_up(\"KeyW\");\n+        sim.run(700.0);\n+        let feet = sim.world().get::<Transform>(\"player\").unwrap().position - Vec3::Y * 0.65;\n+        assert!((feet.y - 1.2).abs() < 0.03, \"feet={feet:?}\");\n+        assert!(feet.x.abs() > 6.5 && feet.x.abs() < 9.5, \"feet={feet:?}\");\n+        assert!(feet.z > 5.5 && feet.z < 8.5, \"feet={feet:?}\");\n+\n+        act(&mut sim);\n+        assert!(sim.world().get::<Lantern>(\"lantern-13\").unwrap().lit);\n+        assert_eq!(sim.world().rows::<Lamp>().filter(|row| row.lantern.lit).count(), 12);\n+        assert_eq!(sim.world().resource::<Session>().phase, 1);\n+\n+        let save = sim.save();\n+        let mut restored = game();\n+        restored.restore(&save).unwrap();\n+        assert!(restored.world().get::<Lantern>(\"lantern-13\").unwrap().lit);\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            restored\n+                .world()\n+                .rows::<Lamp>()\n+                .filter(|row| row.lantern.lit)\n+                .count(),\n+            12\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(restored.world().rows::<Lamp>().count(), 13);\n+        assert_eq!(restored.world().resource::<Session>().phase, 1);\n+    }\n+\n     #[test]\n     fn no_input_loses_at_exactly_three_minutes() {\n         let mut sim = game();\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
